  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe UI link served one client at a time, and the token check only ran\nwhen a complete line arrived. A local client without the token could\nconnect, send no newline, and hold the only session for the 5-minute\n`IDLE_TIMEOUT`, blocking `camcraft-cli --ui`, while the app buffered up\nto 16 MiB (`MAX_LINE`) for it.\n\nTwo new named constants in `crates/app/src/mcp/listen.rs`:\n\n- `PRE_HELLO_DEADLINE`: 5 s. A client that has not sent its hello line\n  within 5 s of connecting is closed. The server writes its warning\n  note (\"no hello line in Ns\") before the drop.\n- `PRE_HELLO_MAX_LINE`: 4 KiB. The buffered-bytes cap before the token\n  check; the drop message stays the existing \"message too long\" line.\n\nIn `serve_client`, the effective idle window is `idle.min(PRE_HELLO_DEADLINE)`\nwhile the gate (the token) is still set, and the room computation and the\npost-read cap check use the pre-hello cap until then. After the hello\npasses, the 5-minute `IDLE_TIMEOUT` and the 16 MiB `MAX_LINE` apply as\nbefore. No behaviour changes for `Inbox::listen` (no token, gate never\nset) or for the in-process channel.\n\nThe busy test's client 1 in `crates/app/tests/mcp_live/ui_link.rs` used\nto simulate a slow call by connecting and staying silent - under the fix\nthat client is dropped after 5 s, so it now sends a real hello line and\nholds the session like a served call. Its asserted behaviour (a second\ncall exits 4, busy) is unchanged.\n\n## The pin\n\n`a_client_that_sends_no_hello_cannot_hold_the_session`\n(`crates/app/tests/mcp_live/ui_link.rs`): client 1 connects and sends\nnothing. Client 2, with the token, retries `link_call` (the link gives\nup exit 4 while the session is held) and is served within seconds - the\nwhole test finishes in about 5.6 s. Without the pre-hello deadline the\nsilent client holds the session for 5 minutes, the retry bound expires,\nand the test fails.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_live ui_link`: 7 passed, 0 failed (5.3 s)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib`: 307 passed, 0 failed (36.8 s)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The Unix-socket transport path of the link (tests run on Windows TCP;\n  the unix arms compile but were not run here).\n- A client that trickles hello bytes past 4 KiB without a newline is\n  covered by the same cap check, but only the no-hello path is pinned\n  by a test.\n- No real `camcraft-cli` binary run against a silent holder beyond what\n  the existing busy test does.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-cli --ui` is no longer blockable for 5 minutes by a\nlocal process that opens the link port and sends nothing.\n\nFixes #3873\n",
